CHAPTER.VERS:
Now when 

          Meaning, the inhabitants of Samaria, whom the king of Assyria had placed in the place of the ten tribes, (2Ki_17:24, 2Ki_19:37). They professed God but worshipped idols and therefore were the greatest enemies to the true servants of God.
         the adversaries of Judah and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity builded the temple unto the LORD God of Israel;

But Zerubbabel, and Jeshua, and the rest of the chief of the fathers of Israel, said unto them, Ye have nothing to do with us to build an house unto our God; 

          For they knew their pretence, that is to erect idolatry instead of true religion.
         but we ourselves together will build unto the LORD God of Israel, as king Cyrus the king of Persia hath commanded us.
